From 57fb04d9bf4ac6ad693d2d335ad5a31c0bebe021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:24:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] ga2: leaner generated VU1 programs (flag liveness,
 threading, entry facts)

- ga2_vu1_gen analyses the whole code image: status flags are dead unless
  FSAND/FSEQ/FSOR exist; an FMAC MAC result is dead when every path
  supersedes it (a later MAC-writing FMAC at least 4 pairs before any
  FMAND/FMEQ/FMOR; program end keeps the last result; JR/JALR count as
  readers). Pairs carry flagMode; values are computed identically.
  GA2_VU1GEN_ALLFLAGS=1 keeps all flags (a strict digest-mode oracle).
- Threaded dispatch: sequential pairs fall through behind one compare.
- PairEntry facts: what the previous image pair (and branches whose delay
  slot carries E/D/T) can leave pending; runs resuming in a delay slot step
  generically first.
- FMAC normalization: single-rounding ops classify from the float result
  (exact path only at 0/FLT_MAX, and only when flags are needed).
- ga2_vu1_replay --reference compares generated programs with this build's
  interpreter (status masked; MAC, run end, data, GIF and cycles compared).
- Warnings when an elided-flag program is followed by another code image or
  hits the cycle budget (the analysis assumptions).

Verified: interpreter vs recorded digests and generated vs interpreter, 0
mismatches on 26k captured runs; all-flags build matches the recorded
digests. Replay 14.3 -> 11.6 ns per VU cycle; in game ~30 -> ~12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
